+# Archive / Cleanup instructions — AgentOptionsTrading
+
+This file explains the safe archival process and the script added at:
+
+  `scripts/move_legacy_to_archive.sh`
+
+### Goal
+
+Safely archive legacy and redundant source files into `src/archive/legacy/` while preserving git history by using `git mv`. This is non-destructive: nothing is permanently deleted until you commit the moves. `refresh_token.py` is explicitly preserved by the script.
+
+### What the script does
+
+- Lists a conservative set of files/folders that are considered legacy (backfill, old tests, duplicate modules).
+- Asks for explicit confirmation (`type YES`) before performing any moves.
+- For each file / folder it:
+  - uses `git mv` to move the path into `src/archive/legacy/<original-relative-path>` (preserves history).
+  - if `git mv` fails it falls back to `cp` + `rm` (less ideal).
+- Skips `src/refresh_token.py` and any other explicit keepers.
+
+### Why we archive rather than delete
+
+1. Preserves git history: `git mv` keeps commits linked to file movement.
+2. Safe rollback: you can restore specific files easily before commit if needed.
+3. Allows manual inspection and selective restore.
+
+### After running
+
+Run:
+
+```bash
+git status --porcelain
+git add -A
+git commit -m "archive: move legacy files to src/archive/legacy"
+```
+
+If you find you moved something by mistake before committing:
+
+```bash
+git mv src/archive/legacy/path/to/file.py src/path/to/file.py
+```
+
+### Files intentionally preserved
+
+- `src/refresh_token.py` (explicit keeper as requested)
+- Keep the files required for the live/paper engine:
+  - `src/live/*` (kite_api.py, kite_data.py, live_paper_engine.py, paper_broker.py)
+  - `src/trading/*` (iron_condor_builder.py, signal_generator.py)
+  - `src/cli/agent_trade.py`
+  - `src/apps/iron_condor_v4.py` (history/backtest)
+  - `src/engine/*` and `src/monitoring/observability.py` (core)
+
+### If you want a one-step removal
+
+After you confirm archived files are safe and committed, you can delete the `src/archive/legacy/` directory in a future commit (if you really want them out of the repo), or keep them as an on-repo archive for traceability.
+
+### Notes
+
+- The script is intentionally conservative. It should be reviewed and run locally.
+- If you want me to produce a direct `git rm` patch instead (destructive), say so explicitly — but I recommend keeping this safer archival flow.
+
+---
